WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
- We have an incredible show today, y'all.

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.260
Joining us is one of the funniest,

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.000
most groundbreaking comedians

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.790
in the history of American
television and film.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:11.910
She's won a Tony, a Grammy, six Emmys,

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.832
and seven Golden Globes,
'cause why the hell not?

00:00:14.832 --> 00:00:15.840
(crowd giggles)

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:16.680
Winning all of them.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.740
She was awarded the
Presidential Medal of Freedom,

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.710
as well as the Mark Twain
Prize for American Humor.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.530
Tonight on NBC, you can
actually watch her tribute,

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:29.130
it's called, "Carol Burnett,
90 Years of Laughter and Love."

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:29.963
It's incredible.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:30.796
(audience applauding)

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:35.331
And today happens to be her 90th birthday.

00:00:35.331 --> 00:00:39.146
Everybody, give it up for
the iconic Carol Burnett.

00:00:39.146 --> 00:00:42.146
(audience cheering)

00:00:43.941 --> 00:00:46.524
(upbeat music)

00:01:01.927 --> 00:01:04.677
(crowd applauds)

00:01:07.994 --> 00:01:08.952
Hello.

00:01:08.952 --> 00:01:10.807
(crowd cheering)

00:01:10.807 --> 00:01:12.191
- Thank you.

00:01:12.191 --> 00:01:14.216
- [Kelly] Keep it coming.

00:01:14.216 --> 00:01:16.774
(crowd cheering)

00:01:16.774 --> 00:01:17.691
Oh my gosh.

00:01:18.905 --> 00:01:19.949
- Thank you.

00:01:19.949 --> 00:01:21.490
- We're so excited you are here.

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:23.040
- [Carol] Oh, I'm so excited to be here.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.040
- I feel like my show just
made it, that you're on it.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:26.873
- Oh God.

00:01:26.873 --> 00:01:28.662
(crowd cheering)

00:01:28.662 --> 00:01:31.560
- We're very excited, today
is a very special day.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.789
Obviously, happy birthday.

00:01:32.789 --> 00:01:33.622
- Thank you.

00:01:33.622 --> 00:01:35.850
- It was my birthday two days ago.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:37.650
- Your birthday is the 24th?

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:38.550
- 24th, yeah.

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:39.383
- And I'm the 26th.

00:01:39.383 --> 00:01:40.216
- [Kelly] 26th, yeah.

00:01:40.216 --> 00:01:42.198
- You're with also Shirley
McClain and Barbara Streisand.

00:01:42.198 --> 00:01:43.920
- Don't you think I know it, girl?

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.099
Yes, I was very excited as a kid, yeah.

00:01:47.099 --> 00:01:49.170
There's a lot of tourists is killing it,

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:50.496
just saying, we're pretty cool.

00:01:50.496 --> 00:01:51.960
We're both from Texas as well.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:52.793
- [Carol] That's right, yeah.

00:01:52.793 --> 00:01:53.940
- Yes, was it San Antonio?

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:54.840
- San Antonio.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.000
- Yeah, do you miss anything?

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.280
Because you were young when
you moved to Hollywood, right?

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.015
- It was back in the covered wagon days.

00:02:01.015 --> 00:02:02.310
(audience laughing)

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.143
- The orange,

00:02:03.143 --> 00:02:05.760
(Kelly giggles)

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.550
- I went to David Crockett Grammar School.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:09.383
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:02:09.383 --> 00:02:10.980
- In San Antonio, yeah.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:11.813
- [Kelly] That's what, I like San Antonio.

00:02:11.813 --> 00:02:13.020
- It was alive then.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.105
- No, it was not.

00:02:14.105 --> 00:02:16.877
(crowd giggles)

00:02:16.877 --> 00:02:18.930
I miss the queso.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.760
I miss chips and queso from Texas.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.593
That's my favorite thing.

00:02:21.593 --> 00:02:23.430
- The best Mexican food ever.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:24.360
- The Tex-Mex, yes.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.590
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:26.423
- [Kelly] I know.

00:02:26.423 --> 00:02:28.170
- That's the first food I remember eating.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.003
- [Kelly] Yeah, 'cause it was.

00:02:29.003 --> 00:02:29.836
- Enchiladas.

00:02:29.836 --> 00:02:30.917
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.870
- Yeah, and then I had my milk, you know.

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:34.590
(crowd giggles)

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:35.490
- Then I had my bottle.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:36.843
- Yeah, bottle of milk.

